## Phase 2: Zero-Copy Iterator

This is the **highest-impact change**. It eliminates deep copies for all internal callers that only READ row data under an existing lock.

### New Method: `ForEachLiveRowUnsafe()`

#### [MODIFY] [table.go](file:///c:/Users/lee.ngari/projects/JoyDb/internal/domain/schema/table.go)

Add a new method:

```go
// ForEachLiveRowUnsafe calls fn for each non-deleted row in PK order.
// The row passed to fn is a direct reference — DO NOT mutate row.Data.
// If fn returns false, iteration stops early.
// MUST be called while holding at least a read lock.
func (t *Table) ForEachLiveRowUnsafe(fn func(row data.Row) bool) {
    if t == nil || t.RowsByRID == nil {
        return
    }

    if t.PKIndex != nil && t.PKIndex.Size() > 0 {
        rids := t.PKIndex.All()
        for _, rid := range rids {
            row, ok := t.RowsByRID[rid]
            if ok && !row.Deleted {
                if !fn(row) {
                    return
                }
            }
        }
        return
    }

    for _, row := range t.RowsByRID {
        if !row.Deleted {
            if !fn(row) {
                return
            }
        }
    }
}
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The row passed to `fn` shares its `Data` map with `RowsByRID`. This is safe because:
> 1. The caller holds a read lock during iteration (no concurrent writes)
> 2. `Table.Update()` uses copy-on-write (creates a new `Data` map before mutation)
> 3. `fn` must NOT mutate `row.Data` — this is enforced by convention and documented

### Callers to Convert

Each caller currently calls `LiveRowsUnsafe()` (materializes ALL rows), then iterates the result. Converting to `ForEachLiveRowUnsafe()` eliminates all intermediate copies.

---

#### [MODIFY] [helpers.go](file:///c:/Users/lee.ngari/projects/JoyDb/internal/query/operations/join/helpers.go)

**`buildJoinIndex()`** — builds a hash index for joins. Only reads `row.Data[columnName]` and `row.RID`. Zero-copy safe.

**Current** (lines 96-103):
```go
hashIndex := make(map[interface{}][]int64)
for _, row := range table.LiveRowsUnsafe() {     // Copies ALL rows
    value, exists := row.Data[columnName]
    if !exists {
        continue
    }
    hashIndex[value] = append(hashIndex[value], row.RID)
}
```

**New:**
```go
hashIndex := make(map[interface{}][]int64)
table.ForEachLiveRowUnsafe(func(row data.Row) bool {
    if value, exists := row.Data[columnName]; exists {
        hashIndex[value] = append(hashIndex[value], row.RID)
    }
    return true
})
```

**Impact:** Eliminates N deep copies per join side. For a 1K×1K join, this saves 2,000 allocations.

---

#### [MODIFY] [foreign_key_validator.go](file:///c:/Users/lee.ngari/projects/JoyDb/internal/executor/foreign_key_validator.go)

**`validateInsertFKs()`** slow path (lines 42-58) — scans parent table to find referenced value. Only reads `pRow.Data[fk.RefColumnName]`. Zero-copy safe.

**Current:**
```go
parentTable.RLock()
for _, pRow := range parentTable.LiveRowsUnsafe() {
    pVal := pRow.Data[fk.RefColumnName]
    if pVal == val { found = true; break }
    // ... numeric normalization check ...
}
parentTable.RUnlock()
```

**New:**
```go
parentTable.RLock()
parentTable.ForEachLiveRowUnsafe(func(pRow data.Row) bool {
    pVal := pRow.Data[fk.RefColumnName]
    if pVal == val { found = true; return false }
    if i1, ok1 := normalizeNumeric(pVal); ok1 {
        if i2, ok2 := normalizeNumeric(val); ok2 {
            if i1 == i2 { found = true; return false }
        }
    }
    return true
})
parentTable.RUnlock()
```

**`validateDeleteFKs()`** (lines 99-119) — same pattern, scans child table. Same conversion.

---

#### [MODIFY] [delete_executor.go](file:///c:/Users/lee.ngari/projects/JoyDb/internal/executor/delete_executor.go)

Two scan loops (lines 17-22 and 34-40) iterate `LiveRowsUnsafe()` to find matching rows. Only need to copy rows that match the predicate.

**Current** (line 17-22):
```go
table.RLock()
var rowsToDelete []data.Row
for _, row := range table.LiveRowsUnsafe() {
    if node.Predicate(row) {
        rowsToDelete = append(rowsToDelete, row.Copy())
    }
}
table.RUnlock()
```

**New:**
```go
table.RLock()
var rowsToDelete []data.Row
table.ForEachLiveRowUnsafe(func(row data.Row) bool {
    if node.Predicate(row) {
        rowsToDelete = append(rowsToDelete, row.Copy())  // Copy only matching rows
    }
    return true
})
table.RUnlock()
```

Same change for the WAL pre-scan at lines 34-40.

---

#### [MODIFY] [update_executor.go](file:///c:/Users/lee.ngari/projects/JoyDb/internal/executor/update_executor.go)

Two scan loops (lines 17-27 and 71-83) — same pattern as delete executor.

---

#### [MODIFY] [executor.go](file:///c:/Users/lee.ngari/projects/JoyDb/internal/query/operations/join/executor.go)

All four join variants (`executeInnerJoin`, `executeLeftJoin`, `executeRightJoin`, `executeFullJoin`) call `leftTable.LiveRowsUnsafe()` to get the probe-side rows.

For INNER JOIN (lines 101-127), the left rows are only read (never mutated). We can iterate without copying:

**Current** (line 101):
```go
leftRows := leftTable.LiveRowsUnsafe()    // Copies ALL left rows
for _, leftRow := range leftRows {
    // ... read leftRow.Data[leftColumn] ...
}
```

**New:**
```go
leftTable.ForEachLiveRowUnsafe(func(leftRow data.Row) bool {
    leftValue, exists := leftRow.Data[leftColumn]
    if !exists {
        return true
    }
    rightRIDs, found := hashIndex[leftValue]
    if !found {
        return true
    }
    for _, rightRID := range rightRIDs {
        rightRow, ok := rightTable.RowsByRID[rightRID]
        if !ok || rightRow.Deleted {
            continue
        }
        joined := combineRows(leftRow, rightRow, leftTable.Name, rightTable.Name)
        if pred == nil || pred(joined) {
            results = append(results, joined)
        }
    }
    return true
})
```

> [!WARNING]
> LEFT/RIGHT/FULL joins need the full `leftRows` slice for the "unmatched rows" phase. These can continue using `LiveRowsUnsafe()` for now, or we can collect unmatched RIDs in the iterator. This is a secondary optimization.

### ✅ Compilation Checkpoint 2
```bash
go build ./...
go test ./...
go run ./cmd/bench --label phase5.2-iterator --duration 5s
```
**Expected:** `join_nested_loop_100_x_100` from ~4,032 to ~8,000-12,000 TPS. FK-heavy benchmarks (`insert_with_fk`) should also improve.

